"What an @service or @externalField reference resolves to, over real Java rather than seeded rows. A reference resolves where exactly one method answers; an overloaded name, a name the class does not declare and a class the reading never reached each resolve to nothing and draw a defect of their own, which is what tells a missing method from a missing class."
type Film @table(name: "film") {
    filmId: ID
    title: String
}

type Query {
    "The overload. One name, two methods, and the resolution refuses to choose between them."
    topRated: [Film!]!
        @service(service: {className: "no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService", method: "topRated"})

    "The ordinary case: one name, one method."
    uppercased: [Film!]!
        @service(service: {className: "no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService", method: "titleUppercase"})

    "A name the class does not declare. The class is read, so the absence is about the method."
    absent: [Film!]!
        @service(service: {className: "no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService", method: "noSuchMethod"})

    "A class nothing on the classpath declares, which is the other cause of the same absence."
    unread: [Film!]!
        @service(service: {className: "no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.NotOnTheClasspath", method: "get"})

    "A service naming no method resolves to nothing, the fallback being the external field's alone."
    unnamed: [Film!]!
        @service(service: {className: "no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService"})
}

extend type Film {
    "The other arm, and the fallback: no method argument, so the field's own name is the method."
    titleUppercase: String
        @externalField(reference: {className: "no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService"})
}

# The whole resolved population of this graph: a reference resolves where exactly one method
# answers, so the overload and the two absences have no row.
extend schema @expectEquals(relation: "graphitron_code_reference", rows: """
  coordinate,          method_name
  Film.titleUppercase, titleUppercase
  Query.uppercased,    titleUppercase
  """)

# Which of the two absences is which. The class behind `absent` was read; the one behind `unread`
# does not exist, so a reader can tell a missing method from a missing class.
extend schema @assertContains(relation: "code_class", rows: """
  class_name
  no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService
  """)

# What each reference that did not resolve draws instead, at the position it was written. The
# service naming no method draws nothing: the fallback to the field's own name is the external
# field's alone. The external field resolves, but to a service method returning no org.jooq.Field,
# which an @externalField cannot call: CODE_REFERENCE_METHOD_UNFIT, pinned by
# defects/external-field-expression and left out here.
extend schema @expectEquals(relation: "graphitron_entry_defect_site",
    where: "code LIKE 'CODE_REFERENCE%' AND code <> 'CODE_REFERENCE_METHOD_UNFIT'", rows: """
  code,                            type_name, field_name, detail
  CODE_REFERENCE_CLASS_NOT_READ,   Query,     unread,     no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.NotOnTheClasspath
  CODE_REFERENCE_METHOD_AMBIGUOUS, Query,     topRated,   no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService.topRated
  CODE_REFERENCE_METHOD_NOT_FOUND, Query,     absent,     no.sikt.graphitron.rewrite.test.services.FilmService.noSuchMethod
  """)
